    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for 2026-07-23 centers on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who provides our highest efficiency floor at a 67.10 score. Facing Legumina and his mediocre 4.32 xERA, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup and an elevated batting order position, making him our primary engine for counting stats today. **Drake Baldwin** also profiles well at 59.15; while he faces a decent arm in Hart, his aggressive spot at the top of the lineup offers the best opportunity for volume, effectively maximizing his ability to contribute to Runs and AVG.\n\nThe remainder of our active lineup carries more risk, as **Brayan Rocchio** (44.53) and **Dominic Smith** (40.68) hover near our marginal start threshold. **Brayan Rocchio** is hampered by the solid 3.82 xERA of Bradley, and **Dominic Smith** suffers from a significant platoon disadvantage against Hart, which drags his efficiency score down toward our bench threshold. While we would typically look to rotate in high-upside speed threats like **Nasim Nunez** or **Cole Carrigg** to address our scarcity in SB, their lack of confirmed starting status keeps them out of the lineup today. **Jackson Merrill** was the closest to cracking the active roster, but his negative platoon splits against Sale combined with a low projected output against an elite arm resulted in a tactical benching to preserve our game caps. \n\nManagement remains cautious regarding the limited volume available, as we are currently without contributions from core roster pieces like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** due to scheduled off-days. We will be monitoring the status of **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Heliot Ramos** closely; should any of them be confirmed into their respective lineups, they may be deployed as late-swaps if **Dominic Smith**\u2019s early performance signals a lackluster output. No major weather concerns are currently flagged, but the lean lineup underscores the importance of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** performing to his ceiling to keep our 5x5 pace steady.",
